---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy — Swarm" description="What swarm-term.com and the Swarm app collect: download and update totals without IP addresses, and email only if you give it.">
  <article class="frame prose privacy">
    <p class="label"># privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short version: no cookies, no tracking, no accounts. We count, we don't follow.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Downloads.</strong> When you click Download, we add one to a daily total for that version and your
        country. Your IP address and browser aren't stored. The file itself then comes from GitHub, which hosts our
        releases, under GitHub's privacy statement.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Release news.</strong> If you subscribe, we keep your email address and the date, and use them only to
        tell you about new versions. Reply to any news email, or write to info@swarm-term.com, and we'll remove it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Issue reports.</strong> The report form emails your report to info@swarm-term.com. The site doesn't
        keep a copy; the email stays in our inbox so we can answer you.
      </li>
      <li>The site uses no cookies and no third-party analytics or fonts. It's hosted on Cloudflare; downloads come from GitHub Releases.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Swarm app</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Update checks.</strong> About once a day, Swarm asks swarm-term.com whether a newer version exists. The
        request says which version you have, and we add one to that version's daily total. Nothing identifies you or
        your Mac.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your sessions.</strong> Terminal sessions, their output and your hosts stay on your Mac and your servers.
        Swarm sends none of it anywhere.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:info@swarm-term.com">info@swarm-term.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .privacy li {
    margin: 10px 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .privacy strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
